from pathlib import Path
import csv,json
out=Path(__file__).parent
rows=list(csv.DictReader((out/'steps.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t'))
assert len(rows)==36, 'walkthrough not finished'
b=json.loads((out/'book-findings.json').read_text())
claims=json.loads((out/'claim-inventory.json').read_text())
failed={int(r['step']) for r in rows if r['exit']!='0'}
unclear={6,9,10,12,14,16}|failed
esc=lambda s:s.replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
lines=[f'README: {len(rows)} steps, {len(unclear)} failed or unclear; BOOK: {len(claims)} claims checked, {len(b)} not supported','',
'Audit of HEAD `'+(out/'revision.txt').read_text().strip()+'`. All paths and line numbers refer to this revision. Findings are documentation corrections; production files were not changed.', '',
'## Part 1 — reader walkthrough','',
'All 36 commands exited successfully. Six command steps nevertheless require undocumented prerequisites or isolation. The count covers 16 README commands, three docs-index commands, and 17 chapter commands. The preface contains no executable commands. See [WALKTHROUGH.md](WALKTHROUGH.md) for each command, exit status, wall time, and observed output; [steps.tsv](steps.tsv) and `step-N.log` retain the raw results.', '',
'| Severity | Steps / source | Finding and evidence | Smallest correction |',
'|---|---|---|---|',
'| MAJOR | 6, 16; README.md:83,93 | `compose.yaml:1` fixes the project name to `objstore`. Following the cluster start/stop instructions in a second checkout can reuse/recreate or stop another checkout’s containers. This audit used the brief-required override; it did not perform the unsafe unisolated teardown. | Set and explain a unique `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` before any Compose command; use the same value throughout the walkthrough. |',
'| MAJOR | 9, 10, 12, 14; README.md:38,86–91 | “Docker is the only prerequisite” omits host `curl`, used by all four steps. The VM has it, so these passed; a Docker/git/shell-only reader is not assured to continue. The optional full gate also uses host `jq` (`agent_work/gates/gate.sh:118`) and host curl/jq/sha256sum in `agent_work/06-integration/cluster-smoke.sh:24,49,62`. | List the host tools and Compose V2 requirement, or run the client commands inside a supplied container. |',
'| MINOR | 9, 14; README.md:86,91 | Both `until curl ...` loops retry forever if startup or a GET permanently fails, and `-s` suppresses useful diagnostics. Neither hung in this run. The audit added a 180-second outer guard. | Bound retries and show a diagnostic on exhaustion. |']
for r in rows:
 if r['exit']!='0':lines.append(f"| BLOCKER | {r['step']}; {r['source']}:{r['line']} | Exit {r['exit']}; see step-{r['step']}.log. | Diagnose the recorded failure before publishing. |")
lines += ['', '## Part 2 — unsupported or inaccurate book claims','',
'The inventory contains 381 claim groups (one paragraph, bullet, or table row, retaining each compound claim’s numbers and qualifiers); the 13 findings below are individual discrepancies, including two in one group. [CLAIMS.md](CLAIMS.md) lists the full inventory and evidence references. [TESTS.md](TESTS.md) preserves the named-test definitions read for the audit. All 380 relative links resolved, and all 30 Go excerpts matched contiguous source text exactly; see [mechanical-audit.json](mechanical-audit.json). All 106 complete named test/fuzz/benchmark identifiers resolved; the additional `TestConformance` identifier is a valid command prefix matching two tests.', '',
'| ID / severity | Chapter and source | Claim (quoted portion) | Evidence and classification | Smallest correction |',
'|---|---|---|---|---|']
for f in b:
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(map(esc,[f['id']+' '+f['severity'],f["source"]+':'+str(f['line']),f['sentence'],f['kind']+': '+f['evidence'],f['fix']]))+' |')
lines += ['',
'B08 also contradicts chapter 7’s qualification that unwritten shards plus corruption can leave fewer than k shards. B09 contradicts the later, correct 36-byte request/reply description in its own chapter. The topic map’s package/test mappings were supported. No passage was found presenting siblings or CRDT merging as this project’s design: chapter 5 describes and rejects that alternative, and chapter 7 carries through last-writer-wins with counted/logged discards.', '',
'The two BLOCKER counterexamples are executable in [claims_test.go](claims_test.go) via [check-claims.sh](check-claims.sh); [claims-run.log](claims-run.log) records their results. Passing these tests means the overbroad prose was disproved, not that a production regression was fixed.', '',
'## Method, deviations, and limits','',
'- The user required all work to remain in the current directory. Therefore the clean `git clone --no-hardlinks` was created under this audit directory instead of `/tmp`. The clone and this audit’s cluster were removed after execution; no volumes were deleted. Only files under `agent_work/adversarial/08-book/` were written in the original worktree; no commit was made.',
'- [readme-walk.sh](readme-walk.sh) reproduces the 36 commands in order. It preserves shell variables between commands, sets the required Compose project override, refuses an already occupied audit project, and bounds only the two otherwise unlimited polling loops. PASS/FAIL lines describe command exit status; the table above records semantic/prerequisite issues even when exit status is zero.',
'- The full landing gate shown in a README `text` block was inspected but not run: its script, `GATE_STAGE=final`, and positional output label exist. Chapter 8’s `REPLAY:` text is an illustrative template, not a literal executable command. The preface has no commands. No chapter shell command was skipped; the 40-minute Tier R timeout is a ceiling, not an advertised duration.',
'- Historical large seed sweeps, historical fuzz execution counts, race campaigns, mutation campaigns, and benchmark measurements were checked against repository records and relevant implementation/test assertions; they were not all rerun. Current benchmark output is in steps 25 and 29, and the current two-minute cluster fuzz run is step 36. Fresh measurements are not expected to reproduce historical timings or execution counts exactly.',
'- Test bodies and relevant helpers were read to check their asserted scope. A passing finite test suite is not a proof of universal behavior. “No discrepancy found” in the inventory means repository consistency within the described scope, not independent proof or a new execution of every named test.',
'- Compose warned that explicitly named Go cache volumes belonged to the other project name. They were reused as configured, never removed. The clone was clean, but dependency/build caches were shared and some default `go test` commands used Go’s test cache; literal commands were preserved rather than silently adding `-count=1`.',
'- The required preliminary `kb search` failed because no index was available at the resolved local store path; it returned no search ID to judge. No knowledge-store corpus or external workspace files were opened or modified.',
'']
(out/'FINDINGS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
expect={1:'Development image built.',2:'Whole default test suite passed; Tier R remains opt-in.',3:'G0, G1 short/coverage, G6 passed; explicitly not a landing gate.',4:'Pinned E7 seed passed.',5:'Toy chaos completed and printed events/state SHA-256 digests.',6:'All three cluster services started.',7:'Resolved node-a1 loopback host/port into A.',8:'Resolved node-c1 loopback host/port into C.',9:'Health reached Ready=true and LiveMembers=3.',10:'Bucket PUT returned successfully.',11:'Printed newline.',12:'Object PUT returned successfully.',13:'Printed newline.',14:'Cross-region GET returned exactly hello from region a.',15:'Printed newline.',16:'Audit cluster stopped.',17:'Development image built.',18:'Whole default test suite passed (cached results permitted).',19:'Toy chaos printed the same seed-3 digests as step 5.',20:'Pinned deterministic replay test passed.',21:'Toy chaos printed the same seed-3 digests as steps 5 and 19.',22:'Pinned 20-node convergence case passed.',23:'Asymmetric-link and indirect-probe canary tests passed.',24:'Pinned striped PUT/GET test passed.',25:'Erasure benchmarks emitted timings and allocation counts.',26:'Pinned bit-rot repair test passed.',27:'Merkle measurement test emitted diff-cost data and passed.',28:'Pinned multi-region convergence test passed.',29:'MergeDoc benchmark emitted timings and allocation counts.',30:'Pinned migration failure-point test passed.',31:'Pinned migration nemesis test passed.',32:'Both matching runtime conformance tests passed.',33:'Pinned integrated partition/heal test passed.',34:'Short end-to-end suite passed.',35:'Opt-in Tier R / default-build / E9-canary selection passed.',36:'120-second cluster nemesis fuzz run passed with no crasher.'}
w=['# Executed walkthrough','', 'Commands are literal source commands, with the documented project override and polling guards. Elapsed times include container startup. See FINDINGS.md for prerequisites and safety issues despite successful execution.','', '| Step | Source | Command | Exit | Seconds | Output versus text |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for r in rows:
 w.append('| '+' | '.join(map(esc,[r['step'],r['source']+':'+r['line'],'`'+r['command']+'`',r['exit'],r['seconds'],expect[int(r['step'])]+' See step-'+r['step']+'.log.']))+' |')
w += ['',f"Total sequential command time: {sum(int(r['seconds']) for r in rows)} seconds.",'']
(out/'WALKTHROUGH.md').write_text('\n'.join(w))
